From d28d3067f1e82b7e1983555ce4d5e1bd1e5647cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:03:07 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] vkr: prefer the physical device sharing the GPU with
 vrend

On multi-GPU hosts the render server's Vulkan instance enumerates the
physical devices in driver order, while vrend, and with it the embedder's
EGL display that imports guest WSI buffers, may be on another GPU, e.g.
the one libvirt picked as QEMU's rendernode. Tiled dma-bufs allocated on
one GPU can generally not be imported by EGL on another one, and linear
ones cross PCIe for every frame.

Send the major/minor of the DRM node vrend uses (get_drm_fd(), i.e. the
EGL display's GPU) to the render server in RENDER_CLIENT_OP_INIT and let
vkr enumerate the matching physical device, and the device group
containing it, first. The physical device is matched through
VK_EXT_physical_device_drm.

The fields are appended to render_client_op_init_request. The server
accepts the old request size, so an older client keeps the driver order.
An older server rejects the larger request, so the client and the server
have to be updated together.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
